WEBVTT

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.900
Very difficult to believe.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.950
I feel the same way.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.820
I heard it, but I still don't believe it.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:06.320
...more about my...

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.390
...myself.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.800
This is...

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.100
What?

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.330
Who?

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.900
Could it be Frank's voice?

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.300
Nah, can't be.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.640
What frequency?

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:24.090
SW, short wave radio.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.880
I want to know... myself.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.250
Run a trace.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.760
Find out where it's from.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.410
Quickly!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:43.960
And you concluded that the voice
originated from the EX-1?

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.120
Yes.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.030
Do the others know?

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.540
Not yet. I told Lt. Harris it
was a matter of top security.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.540
If you were a car dealer, for example...

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.940
...and the cars on display
began talking, what would you do?

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:06.650
"My engine will break down soon."
"I've had a lot of work done."

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.640
"I'm a lemon."

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.830
It'd be hard on the buyers, too.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.130
I suppose so.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:19.500
Even among humans, words
can create misunderstanding.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:24.270
Sometimes we find out things
we were better off not knowing.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.380
No, I guess it all depends on the listener.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.920
It's a heavy burden.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:41.460
In any case, we must proceed carefully.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:45.660
This may warrant a rethinking
of how we fight the aliens-

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.360
What is it?

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.100
HQ on the line.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.830
Hattie!

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.660
Why...

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.930
Could it be you...

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.110
No, I...

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.610
No!

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:39.440
Lt. Ryu Soma, code 357.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.350
Please, return to full alert.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.370
Which unit is Funeral supposed
to provide an escort for?

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.860
Nobody told you?

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:58.160
One of the new model intercept
fighters from Zone 21, Alaska.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.730
Zone 21...

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:00.790
Isn't that...

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.270
Right, Ryu's former station.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.630
Got the signal.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.380
Looks pretty bad.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.280
Contact established.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.950
Escort proceeding to runway three.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.260
An unexpected guest.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.340
It was an official rescue request.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.240
We couldn't say no.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:37.570
And what about that alien in the stratosphere?

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.670
No order to intercept yet.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:48.350
In any event, it's like
a badminton birdie stuck in a tree.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.320
We don't have a stick long
enough to knock it down.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.070
A stratospheric intercept pilot?

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.830
Pretty elite, huh?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.580
If he counts, so do we.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:17.410
Ha ha ha.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.810
No conviction at all.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.850
Because you've got punks like me in the ranks.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.320
I didn't say...

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.680
Absolutely incredible!

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.160
I must be in heaven!

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.060
Pretty angel...

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.700
...what's your name?

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:41.000
Tell Rick Steiner.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.570
Please!

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.240
Rick?

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:46.770
And let's not forget this angel.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:51.570
Excuse me...

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.170
No, pardon me.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:56.290
I couldn't help myself
before all these lovely ladies.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:04.760
Alaskan border, Zone 21
Intercept Fighter Division...

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.510
...2nd Lt. Rick Steiner, at your service.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:11.130
Rick, you haven't changed a bit.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.000
The guy's a pain.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.630
In the aerospace test...

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:18.330
Hey, Takuto!

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.540
Don't trash talk people
when they're not around.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.370
Way to go, Takuto.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.720
What?

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.620
I heard a lot about you.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.250
Maki Agata, right?

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.880
Y-Yes.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.970
Just like Takuto said.

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:47.160
An adorable angel in glasses.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.130
No, I'm really not...

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.020
Lt. Soma!

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.940
Let me introduce you. Come here.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.710
Your former station was Zone 21, wasn't it?

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:05.370
It's Lt. Steiner.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.800
Do you know Lt. Soma?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.340
No, I just transferred over.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.100
Is that so.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.970
Well, Ryu keeps to himself...

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.880
...so there probably aren't
many who get to know him.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:31.610
Don't be rude, Sue.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.380
About your aircraft...

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:38.440
We can do emergency repairs
and refuel it, but I'm afraid...

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:39.750
That's enough.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:41.570
All I need is to be able to fly.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.530
Then I'll take you to our waiting area.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:13.380
Don't be an idiot, Takuto.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.730
You've got a pretty girlfriend.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.660
I know. You don't have to tell me.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:23.460
Guys like you get all the good
ones and ruin it for the rest of us.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:25.330
That's not true.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:30.860
Nope, they'll always go for
the cool type like you in a pinch.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.930
Hey, this is a simulation.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.480
Cut the chatter!

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:36.710
Cock Robin here.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:40.310
We've had an accident. Communications are out.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.690
Anyway, keep your mouth shut.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:47.180
But...

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:52.400
Don't tell the truth, and it didn't happen.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.390
Understand?

00:10:57.030 --> 00:11:00.400
If you care about Maki,
take it with you to the grave.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.960
Okay, Takuto?

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.660
So your uniforms are original to this base?

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.220
That's right.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:32.170
Guess your commander likes girls in uniform.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.730
Sorry, but our commander's a woman.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:36.440
A woman commander?

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:40.110
What's she like? Big, scary old lady?

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:43.040
She can be scary, I suppose, right?

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:44.480
She's very pretty.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.450
Oh, Jesus!

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:49.620
Mine's an old, ugly dude with a big mustache.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.090
It's not fair, God!

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.410
Ryu!

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:02.900
Sue just gave me a whole bunch of snacks.

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.190
You want some?

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.300
Th-The same face...

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.210
The same face...

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.340
Exactly the same face.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.580
The same face, the same face...

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.590
Little Maki.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.970
You look just like my college
buddy's girlfriend Maki.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.190
Maki?

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.070
So sweet and warm.

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:51.560
An angel's heavenly warmth.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.640
Ryu, who is this man?

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.650
Don't worry, he's just some soldier.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:57.950
Hey, wait.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.750
Do I look like someone named Maki?

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.610
Beautiful stars out here, too.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.540
Not quite like Alaska's, though.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.720
Gagarin.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:37.090
Shepard.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.150
Walker.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.290
Armstrong.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.700
Lovell, Young, Borman.

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:44.930
And Yuri Leonov of the Odysseus.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:47.870
Do you know them?

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:49.800
They're astronauts, right?

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:50.860
Correct.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:03.250
You're the same.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.430
The same as a college buddy of mine.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.350
You're imagining things.

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.170
Not your appearance.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.750
It's that faraway look when
you're watching the stars.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.970
You know, Lieutenant...

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.030
I always wanted to go up there.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:28.940
To see how the air smells on Mars.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:34.580
How magnificent that festival
of satellites is around Jupiter.

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:39.090
To find out if aliens forgot
something in the rings of Saturn.

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:40.890
Sound childish?

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:48.190
I used to talk about these things
with my buddy all the time.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:50.320
What happened to him?

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:51.700
He died.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:54.260
After I got picked up by the army.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:56.810
He was killed in a freak accident.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.170
And that's why...

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:04.780
...I fly that modern killer machine
with missiles, radar, and all.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.450
I have to fly his share, too!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.820
I think that's why...

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:12.160
Cool, aren't I?

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.190
No, not really.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.890
How can you say that, Lieutenant?

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:24.630
Everything within range has been destroyed.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:27.360
There's no reason for the attack, or...

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.520
Baalzephon Division 11, damage at 85%.

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:35.060
Early warning satellite ES-22 is destroyed.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:39.910
Could it be the alien is clearing a path for others?

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.680
Like a mine sweeper?

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:44.150
Commander, message from HQ.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:44.910
Read it.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:48.420
A Florida base will launch a nuclear attack

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.120
using stratospheric missiles.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.370
Launch time is scheduled at 2340.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.190
Two hours from now.

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:57.590
It'll be too late.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.830
Their efforts are wasted, as usual.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:05.670
Generator Satellite Icarus will pass
Ulysses' orbit in 46 minutes...

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:08.010
...putting it in the alien's firing range.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:13.130
So that monument of the space
age will be turned to space dust.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.060
It can't be...

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:18.080
Ulysses may break up over populated areas.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.530
Careful radar monitoring advised.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:22.950
Ulysses...

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:29.350
You can't!

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.700
We haven't added the propellant!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.500
What happened?

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:43.070
He just suddenly demanded
clearance for takeoff.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.040
Who?

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.370
This is SARG 5.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:09.790
It's Lt. Soma.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.930
You're off course, Lt. Steiner!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.840
The Alaska base is the other way.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:18.980
Correct, I'm initiating the
stratospheric intercept sequence.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.980
You didn't get an order. Stop!

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.890
Lieutenant, why are you...

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:32.550
Ulysses.

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:35.960
Mankind's first deep space probe.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:39.780
The Odysseus deployed it,
vanishing with Yuri Leonov...

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:43.670
...the 21st century's most famous astronaut.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:44.760
I know.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:46.600
I know all that.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:49.290
They abandoned it during renovations.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:53.640
Now it'll be destroyed by
this alien we didn't kill earlier.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:56.350
That's why I'm going.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.130
Then I'll back you up.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:02.290
That may be Funeral's finest,
but its cockpit isn't made for this.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.350
You can't.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.830
Don't worry.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.960
This isn't a suicide mission.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.630
This baby's ace is a nuclear AP.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.400
If I can hit the target...

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:18.980
Stay low and watch.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:28.380
Target sighted.

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:30.520
Can you hear me, Lieutenant?

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:32.920
Not well, but I can make it out.

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.020
About my buddy...

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:39.460
His girlfriend...

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:42.130
I liked her, too, you know.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.230
What are you talking about?

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:46.130
Just listen.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:49.140
I kinda forced my friend to betray her.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:54.780
Then I told him we'd keep it a secret...

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.750
...but I let her find out about the affair.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.480
I always wanted to apologize...

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:08.830
...for so long.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.930
But now he's gone.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:18.700
We had good times flying and testing together.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:21.700
We qualified in only one run.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:31.040
That was the first time I saw the
Ulysses as it was being worked on.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.480
Why are you telling me?

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:34.970
Because...

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.330
Lt. Steiner!

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:01.140
Come in!

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:02.370
Please!

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:14.320
Rick...

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.680
The surveillance system has been shut down.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.670
Listed as under inspection in the logs.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:48.250
Men, what you see and hear now
does not go beyond our members.

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.230
Go ahead, Harriet.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.510
Mr. Fairy, do you understand what I'm saying?

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:28.460
Mr. Fairy?

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:30.860
That's right!

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.100
You understand?

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:33.960
Thank you...

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:39.340
I don't know what you mean, Mr. Fairy.

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:41.000
I...

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.240
Where...

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.200
I don't know...

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:23.780
Y-You...

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:40.400
A bird with broken wings
will die watching the sky.

00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:45.010
As it dreams of the forest
from which it came...

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:48.810
Next time,
The Past and Crimes.
